 `add`, `rename` and `tag` reject invalid input with an `invalid-input` error whose message says what is
 wrong, and leave the list unchanged: a title that is empty or only spaces, or longer than 120 characters
 (after trimming); a priority other than `low`, `normal` or `high`; a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+
+## Bulk import
+
+`importTasks(list, text)` adds tasks from text, one per line as `title;priority;tags`, for example
+`Renew the insurance;high;admin money`. The priority may be empty for a normal one, tags are separated by
+spaces, and trailing fields may be left out. Blank lines are skipped. It returns `{ imported, rejected }`:
+`imported` counts the tasks added, and `rejected` lists each line that could not be added as
+`{ line, reason }`, with `line` counting from 1 (blank lines count). A line is rejected for the reasons
+under "Input rules", for a title already in the list (or earlier in the text), or for more than three
+fields. Rejected lines do not stop the others from being added.
